  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "105",
  "quote": "The only security deposit that a landlord may collect is a rent deposit collected in accordance with section 106.",
  "reason": "The Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 prohibits landlords from collecting any security deposit other than a rent deposit for last month's rent. Because a pet damage deposit is not a rent deposit, a clause requiring it is inconsistent with section 105 and therefore void under section 4."
}

